
# PENDING — this section is deliberately empty.
#
# makeResult needs a ctx carrying a constructed Spec AND Result (built via the
# SDK's own NewSpec/NewResult constructors), plus the error path for each being
# absent. The shared runner builds a ctx from a literal map and has no
# constructor hook, so the cases cannot be expressed here yet. Covered
# per-language today (e.g. go's makeResult-basic / -no-spec / -no-result),
# which is exactly the drift risk this corpus exists to remove — promoting it
# needs a runner change, not just fixture data.
#
# An empty `set` runs ZERO cases. Runners must not treat that as a pass by
# accident: test/corpus.test.ts here, and the PENDING lists in the language
# runners, keep a deliberately-deferred section distinct from an accidentally
# blanked one.

basic: set: []
